implementationPlan.description:
Rows SF1-SF4 in scripts/tests/local-runner-seat.test.mjs, which CQ-M07i created; edit it, never recreate it. First grep `test('SF`: it was unused at planning. M07i owns AS0-AS6 and CQ-M07j will add SJ1-SJ5. Import seatForward beside M07i's agent-seat.mjs import.
Helpers, named sf* so they cannot clash with M07i's (reuse an equivalent if M07i already added one):
- sfHealth(t, project, { listen = '127.0.0.1', report = listen, onRequest } = {}): a node:http server on listen:0 that answers /health with { status: 'healthy', projectPath: project, bindHost: report }. It counts hits, calls onRequest, resolves port 0 where the host cannot bind (VC-M1 healthOn), and closes in t.after (closeAllConnections + close).
- sfSocket(...): VC-M1's EventTarget FakeSocket. It records its constructor arguments, every sent frame (parsed) and close() calls. By default it dispatches 'open' in a microtask; a row can script the construct phase (e.g. 'error' instead of 'open') and the after-send phase. Use new Event('open'|'close'|'error') and new MessageEvent('message', { data }).
- daemon.json is { port, pid: 1, startedAt: 'x', projectPath: project } under a scratch project's .moe/.
SF1 (DoD 1), transport and raw result:
- forward('moe.acquire_resource', { resourceId: 'r', taskId: 'task-a', workerId: 'w' }, { signal }), with a live AbortController signal, resolves the raw result deepStrictEqual to the one the fake sent, NOT the parsed text. That result carries an extra member, e.g. { content: [{ type: 'text', text: '{"granted":true}' }], structuredContent: { k: 1 } }.
- Exactly one socket. Its constructor arguments deep-equal [`ws://127.0.0.1:${port}/mcp`]. sent deep-equals [{ jsonrpc: '2.0', id: 1, method: 'tools/call', params: { name: 'moe.acquire_resource', arguments: <the args verbatim> } }]. closed === 1. getEventListeners(signal, 'abort') (node:events) is empty after the resolve.
- Two concurrent calls on the same forward: two sockets, ids 2 and 3, one frame each, and each resolves its own reply. The fake echoes the call's arguments in its text.
- ::1: with daemon.json bindHost '::1' and a ::1 /health, the URL is ws://[::1]:<port>/mcp. Where ::1 cannot bind, emit t.diagnostic and skip that part (VC-M1).
SF2 (DoD 2): every failure rejects with code SEAT_FORWARD_FAILED and a message free of the daemon's text ('/secret').
- Give the test { timeout: 10_000 } and the forward timeoutMs 60_000, so only the event under test can reject. A mutant that drops a listener then fails by test timeout instead of hanging.
- Socket rows, each asserting made.length === 1 and made[0].closed === 1:
  - an error reply { error: { code: -32602, message: '/secret', data: { codeName: 'NOT_FOUND' } } };
  - a 'close' event with no reply;
  - an 'error' event instead of 'open';
  - non-JSON data;
  - { result: null };
  - a reply under another id, then silence, with timeoutMs 20: it must reject, never resolve that reply;
  - silence with timeoutMs 20 (the timeout), after which the abort listener list is empty;
  - silence, then the send hook aborts the controller (abort mid-call).
- Pre-socket refusals, each asserting made.length === 0 where a fake is supplied:
  - AbortSignal.abort() already aborted, with zero /health hits;
  - a /health onRequest that aborts the controller (abort during the probe: one hit, no socket);
  - args { n: 1n }, which cannot be serialized;
  - WebSocketImpl null;
  - a constructor that throws new Error('/secret') (code only).
SF3 (DoD 3), no key and no headers:
- Register the env restore with t.after BEFORE mutating env (gotcha), then point MOE_RUNNER_KEY_DIR at path.join(<scratch>, 'missing').
- The same call resolves the same raw result, the constructor saw exactly one argument (the URL), and the sent frames are identical to a run without the variable.
SF4 (DoD 4): refusal before any socket, through readDaemonInfo. Each case gives made.length === 0 and SEAT_FORWARD_FAILED:
- a daemon.json naming another project (path.join(project, 'other')) while /health is healthy for this one;
- a /health reporting bindHost '0.0.0.0' for this project;
- a daemon.json with bindHost '0.0.0.0';
- no daemon.json.
No platform skips: M07i put this file in ci.yml, so it runs on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs. Keep the rows table-driven, within about 160 lines.
